    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Yordan Alvarez** (77.56). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, benefiting from a +14% dynamic platoon boost against Pfaadt and a +4% edge for exploiting the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which is critical given our heavy weighting on stolen bases. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a core anchor; despite a standard park adjustment, his elite 0.458 xwOBA and favorable lineup spot provide a floor that few others can replicate. **Junior Caminero** (76.90) also warrants attention, as he faces a mid-tier arm in Jobe and enjoys the combination of a high-leverage #3 spot in the order and a favorable park factor, rounding out a formidable top-tier quartet.\n\nWhile we are aggressive in the outfield, the decision to bench **Chase Meidroth** (37.20) was the most difficult pivot of the day. Despite his base profile, the matchup against the elite arm of deGrom (3.05 xERA) decimated his projected efficiency, forcing a -19% penalty to his SP Skill metric and pushing him below our 40.0 floor. We have similarly relegated **Carson Benge** (34.33) to the bench due to a brutal platoon disadvantage and an equally daunting matchup against Harrison. We are keeping a close watch on **Dillon Dingler** (43.97) and **Jacob Gonzalez** (47.71); both are barely above the threshold, and their production will be monitored closely to ensure we preserve our remaining game caps for higher-leverage situations later this week.",
